            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz</strong><br>\nGottfried Wilhelm Leibniz was born on July 1, 1646, in Leipzig, Germany. He grew up in a time of intense intellectual ferment and war. By the age of twelve, he had taught himself Latin and was already learning Greek. His early education was steeped in philosophy and law, which paved the way for his future contributions to a variety of academic fields. Leibniz's fascination with the world of academia was evident from his early years, hinting at the polymath he would become.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Mathematics</strong><br>\nLeibniz made significant contributions to mathematics that have had a lasting impact. He is best known for developing the calculus independently of Isaac Newton. His notation for calculus is still in use today. Leibniz's work in mathematics wasn't just limited to calculus; he also worked on binary numbers and systematized much of probability theory, reflecting his profound understanding of the subject.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Philosophy and Rationalism</strong><br>\nAs a philosopher, Leibniz was a major figure in rationalism. He proposed that ours is the best of all possible worlds, a concept that later philosophers and writers either supported or mocked. Leibniz's belief in a logical and orderly universe led him to argue that reality consists of monads, which are simple substances that form the fabric of the universe. His philosophies addressed issues such as free will, the nature of God, and the problem of evil.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
